            <div xml:id="d246">

                <pb facs="0312" n="300" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg300"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/10149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé at Tangier</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Childs</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-04-21T12:00:00+01:00">April 21,
                            1941—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 4:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>107. I was informed by Meyrier, the principal assistant to Noguès in Rabat, that
                    Hitler had said privately recently the following in substance: “I know what is
                    going on in French North Africa. That does not disturb me. I know precisely how
                    many tanks and planes the French have there and I can crush in 3 days any
                    movement that raises its head there.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Childs</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
